{"type":"assistant","uuid":"57a5595c-8086-4e36-b888-f6046f917321","session_id":"1758ab42-d9c9-4967-876d-1c3efc95e0a9","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"57a5595c-8086-4e36-b888-f6046f917321","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nBoth changes are confirmed in place. Here's the summary of the fix:\n\n## Summary\n\n### Root Cause\nThe bug is a **race condition in initialization order**. When `IntroScreenActivity` creates both fragments:\n\n1. `EncryptionFragment`'s `onCreateView()` runs first and sets the spinner to `PASSWORD` (the hardcoded default)\n2. This triggers a callback to `AuthenticationFragment.updateEncryptionType(PASSWORD)`, but `AuthenticationFragment`'s `onCreateView()` **hasn't run yet**, so `desc` is `null` and the text never gets set\n3. When the user navigates to slide 3, `AuthenticationFragment.onCreateView()` runs with `encryptionType = KEYSTORE` (the hardcoded field default), showing the wrong description\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Activities/IntroScreenActivity.java`\n\n| Change | Line | What |\n|--------|------|------|\n| **Fix 1** | ~77 | `saveSettings()` now stores empty string for `AuthMethod.NONE` (defensive) |\n| **Fix 2** | ~435-447 | `AuthenticationFragment.onCreateView()` now initializes `desc` and spinner based on the actual `encryptionType` (which was set by the callback), instead of unconditionally defaulting to `PASSWORD` |\n\n### Behavior Before Fix\n- Default: Encryption=PASSWORD (selected) → Auth desc shows KEYSTORE text (wrong)\n- If user switches to KEYSTORE → Auth desc updates to KEYSTORE text (correct)\n\n### Behavior After Fix\n- Default: Encryption=PASSWORD (selected) → Auth desc shows PASSWORD text (correct), spinner defaults to PASSWORD\n- If user switches to KEYSTORE → Auth desc shows KEYSTORE text, spinner defaults to NONE (since auth is optional)"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48818,"output_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":48208,"total_tokens":49237}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"3f1e2875-8d62-4dae-a811-c47b6add37c3","session_id":"1758ab42-d9c9-4967-876d-1c3efc95e0a9","is_error":false,"duration_ms":124360,"duration_api_ms":93225,"num_turns":31,"result":"\n\nBoth changes are confirmed in place. Here's the summary of the fix:\n\n## Summary\n\n### Root Cause\nThe bug is a **race condition in initialization order**. When `IntroScreenActivity` creates both fragments:\n\n1. `EncryptionFragment`'s `onCreateView()` runs first and sets the spinner to `PASSWORD` (the hardcoded default)\n2. This triggers a callback to `AuthenticationFragment.updateEncryptionType(PASSWORD)`, but `AuthenticationFragment`'s `onCreateView()` **hasn't run yet**, so `desc` is `null` and the text never gets set\n3. When the user navigates to slide 3, `AuthenticationFragment.onCreateView()` runs with `encryptionType = KEYSTORE` (the hardcoded field default), showing the wrong description\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Activities/IntroScreenActivity.java`\n\n| Change | Line | What |\n|--------|------|------|\n| **Fix 1** | ~77 | `saveSettings()` now stores empty string for `AuthMethod.NONE` (defensive) |\n| **Fix 2** | ~435-447 | `AuthenticationFragment.onCreateView()` now initializes `desc` and spinner based on the actual `encryptionType` (which was set by the callback), instead of unconditionally defaulting to `PASSWORD` |\n\n### Behavior Before Fix\n- Default: Encryption=PASSWORD (selected) → Auth desc shows KEYSTORE text (wrong)\n- If user switches to KEYSTORE → Auth desc updates to KEYSTORE text (correct)\n\n### Behavior After Fix\n- Default: Encryption=PASSWORD (selected) → Auth desc shows PASSWORD text (correct), spinner defaults to PASSWORD\n- If user switches to KEYSTORE → Auth desc shows KEYSTORE text, spinner defaults to NONE (since auth is optional)","usage":{"input_tokens":1559073,"output_tokens":19686,"cache_read_input_tokens":1398032,"total_tokens":1578759},"permission_denials":[]}
